        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "207e6203-2ffd-5267-9d62-d6fb9ad9cbd8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michelle Dockery, Dan Stevens, Colin Wratten\n- Works: The Turn of the Screw (2009 film), Downton Abbey, The Musketeers, Inside Men, Waking the Dead, EastEnders\n- Roles: Ann, Dr Fisher, Lady Mary Crawley\n- Organizations: BBC, ITV, PBS, Emmy Awards, Golden Globe Awards\n\nFacts:\n- In the 2009 film The Turn of the Screw, the story is told in flashbacks during consultations between the institutionalised Ann, played by Michelle Dockery, and Dr Fisher, played by Dan Stevens.\n- From 2010 to 2015, Michelle Dockery was widely known for playing Lady Mary Crawley in the television period drama series Downton Abbey, which aired on ITV in the UK and PBS in the U.S.\n- Michelle Dockery received three consecutive Emmy Award nominations for Outstanding Lead Actress in a Drama Series and one Golden Globe Award nomination for Downton Abbey.\n- Colin Wratten produced the BBC television film The Turn of the Screw.\n- Colin Wratten also produced episodes of the BBC dramas The Musketeers, Inside Men, and Waking the Dead, as well as episodes of the BBC soap EastEnders.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "24205ad2-e841-5940-b4a6-e65484ecc0bf",
        "text": "Page: The Turn of the Screw (2009 film). Sentence: The film's story is told in flashbacks during consultations between the institutionalised Ann (Michelle Dockery) and Dr Fisher (Dan Stevens).\nPage: Michelle Dockery. Sentence: She is most widely known for her performance as Lady Mary Crawley in the ITV (UK) and PBS (U.S.) television period drama series \"Downton Abbey\" (2010–15), for which she was nominated for three consecutive Emmy Awards in the category for Outstanding Lead Actress In Drama Series, and a Golden Globe Award nomination.\nPage: Colin Wratten. Sentence: He has produced episodes of BBC dramas \"The Musketeers\", \"Inside Men\" and \"Waking the Dead\", as well as BBC television film \"The Turn of the Screw\" and episodes of BBC soap \"EastEnders\".",
